		"note": "`POST /v3/cluster/member/remove` takes `{\"ID\":\"<id>\"}` and answers with the list that is left. The id is the decimal form of the 64-bit number in this list — `name` is a label and `peerURLs` can be edited, so neither identifies anything. An example cannot run the removal without shrinking the cluster every later example shares, so what it shows is the lookup: find the id here, send it there. Note that the number is a JSON string, as every 64-bit field on this wire is.",
